     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO TID is 5100 mg/day.** That's about twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2550 mg/day (850 mg TID) in U.S. labeling. Exceeding the maximum raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. The patient's normal renal and hepatic function doesn't change the ceiling. Also, 1700 mg doesn't match a standard tablet strength (500, 850, or 1000 mg IR).\n\nSome possible intents:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2550 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1500 mg/day, a common starting dose)\n- **1700 mg PO daily** with the evening meal, if you want a once-daily ER formulation (ER maximum is 2000 mg/day)\n- A deliberate dose above usual limits, if you have a specific reason\n\nPlease tell me which regimen you want, or confirm the original order if 5100 mg/day is intentional. I'll enter it once you confirm."
      }
     ],
